    body: "Congratulations! You are officially under contract! We're so excited to help get you to the closing table!\n\nMy name is {{transaction_coordinator_full_name}} and I'm the Transaction Coordinator for {{buyers_agent_full_name}}. I will be in contact moving forward, but they will continue to handle any negotiations and amendments. To ensure we get to the closing table smoothly and efficiently, you will be hearing from me periodically with updates and reminders.\n\nI have attached a copy of the fully executed contract docs. You can expect to continue to receive docs from {{primary_agent}} or me for your signatures as we continue to move towards closing.\n\n{{primary_agent}} has let me know that you won't be in town during the transaction process. We can handle the entire transaction digitally however, the Final Documents need to be signed in front of a notary. The title company can send a mobile notary to help you with that, or you can use a notary of your choice. You can also reach out to us if you have any questions. We are here to help make this transaction as smooth and easy as possible for you.\n\nTransaction info:\n- Acceptance Date: {{contract_date}}\n- Funding Type: {{financing_type}}\n- Purchase Price: {{purchase_amount}}\n- Seller Concession %: {{seller_concession_percentage}}\n- Seller Concession $: {{seller_concession_amount}}\n- Earnest Money Amount: {{earnest_money_amount}}\n- Earnest Money Holder: {{title_officer_business_name}}\n- Inspection Period: {{inspection_contingency_date}}\n- Inspection Period: WAIVED\n- Close of Escrow: {{smart_block_timeline_on_or_before_closing}}{{closing_date}}\n- Possession Date: {{possession_date}}\n\nTitle Company:\n[START_CONTACT]\n{{title_officer_business_name}}\n{{title_officer_business_address}}\n{{title_officer_full_name}} {{title_officer_phone}}\n{{title_officer_email}}\n [END_CONTACT]\n\n*You will receive calls and emails from the title company. To ensure we get to the closing table on time, please make sure to complete any of their requests as soon as possible.\n\n*Your next steps:\n\nWire Your Earnest Money Deposit: I've requested that the title company reach out to you as soon as possible with instructions to deposit your earnest money. If a few days go by and you have not heard from them, or if you'd like to change the method of depositing your earnest money, please let me know.\n\nAttending the Home Inspection (optional): To prepare for this, you can review the Residential Property Disclosure Statement and make note of any questions you may have for the inspector. This is also a great time to drive the neighborhood and visit stores or parks in the area.\n\nNegotiations: We can expect the inspection report within a few days after the inspection takes place. You'll hear from {{primary_agent}} to review and discuss it once received. If there are any concerns you would like the seller to address, a repair request will be drafted and an agreement must be made by the inspection period end date ({{inspection_contingency_date}}). If an agreement is not made by this day, you and the seller could agree to extend this period, or you have the opportunity to terminate.\n\nRemoval of Contingency: Once the inspection period is concluded, the seller will get to work on your requests (if any). There are quite a few steps after that, but I'll be sure to touch base with more information on what's to come.\n\nWorking with your Lender: Continue working together to get them all the necessary documents so that they can get moving on your loan. Any delays in getting them what they need could potentially delay the closing.\n\n*Important* - Any financial changes will affect your credit and ability to close on this property. Please do not make any large purchases, move funds, or do anything that will have your credit pulled/checked without discussing the issues or possible ramifications with your lender. Please see the \"10 Commandments\" attached for more info!\n\nPlease feel free to call, text, or email me with any questions or concerns. I am here to help!",
